foundation.question_text:
Every side of this triangle is $6$ cm and every angle is $60^{\circ}$. Is it regular or irregular?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0); \coordinate (B) at (4,0); \coordinate (C) at (2,3.464);
\draw (A) -- (B) node[midway,below] {$6\text{ cm}$};
\draw (B) -- (C) node[midway,above right] {$6\text{ cm}$};
\draw (C) -- (A) node[midway,above left] {$6\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Every side of this square is $4$ cm and every angle is $90^{\circ}$. Is it regular or irregular?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (0,0) rectangle (3.4,3.4);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

This rhombus has four equal sides, but it has two $70^{\circ}$ angles and two $110^{\circ}$ angles. Is it regular or irregular?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (0,-1.5) -- (2.9,0) -- (0,1.5) -- (-2.9,0) -- cycle;
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

This rectangle has four equal angles. Its side lengths are $7$ cm, $3$ cm, $7$ cm and $3$ cm. Is it regular or irregular?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0); \coordinate (B) at (5,0); \coordinate (C) at (5,2.2); \coordinate (D) at (0,2.2);
\draw (A) -- (B) node[midway,below] {$7\text{ cm}$};
\draw (B) -- (C) node[midway,right] {$3\text{ cm}$};
\draw (C) -- (D) node[midway,above] {$7\text{ cm}$};
\draw (D) -- (A) node[midway,left] {$3\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Four sides of this pentagon are $5$ cm and one side is $4$ cm. Is it regular or irregular?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.8]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0); \coordinate (B) at (3.2,0); \coordinate (C) at (5,3.572); \coordinate (D) at (1.6,5.679); \coordinate (E) at (-1.8,3.572);
\draw (A) -- (B) node[midway,below] {$4\text{ cm}$};
\draw (B) -- (C) node[midway,right] {$5\text{ cm}$};
\draw (C) -- (D) node[midway,above right] {$5\text{ cm}$};
\draw (D) -- (E) node[midway,above left] {$5\text{ cm}$};
\draw (E) -- (A) node[midway,left] {$5\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The sides of this hexagon are all equal, but its interior angles are not all equal. Is it regular or irregular?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (0,0) -- (2,0) -- (3,1.732) -- (1,1.732) -- (0,3.464) -- (-1,1.732) -- cycle;
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

development.question_text:
A hexagon has six equal sides and six equal angles. Classify it as regular or irregular.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\foreach \i in {0,...,5} {\coordinate (P\i) at ({60*\i}:2.4);}
\draw (P0) -- (P1) -- (P2) -- (P3) -- (P4) -- (P5) -- cycle;
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Noah measures all four sides of this quadrilateral and finds that they are equal. He immediately labels it regular. Explain why he does not yet have enough information.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (0,-1.5) -- (2.9,0) -- (0,1.5) -- (-2.9,0) -- cycle;
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
